---
import './freshness.css';
---
<figure class="fresh-figure" data-fresh-race>
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 2</span>The last fill wins</div>
 <div class="controls"><label>After the source commit <select data-action><option value="delete">Delete the cached key</option><option value="update">Write revision 2 to the cache</option></select></label></div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="journey" aria-hidden="true">
   <svg viewBox="0 0 600 150" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M300 35 L90 105 L510 105" /></svg>
   <span class="station source">Source</span><span class="station reader">App A</span><span class="station cache">Cache</span>
   <span class="packet" data-packet>rev 1</span>
  </div>
  <div class="row" data-live>
   <div class="box"><p class="label">Authoritative source</p><strong data-source>GBP 20.00 · revision 1</strong></div>
   <div class="box"><p class="label">Cache · P7</p><strong data-cache>Empty</strong><span data-ttl>No entry</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="lane"><p class="label">App A · reading the card</p><p data-reader data-live>Has not read the source yet.</p></div>
  <div class="lane"><p class="label">App B · changing the price</p><p data-writer data-live>Has not changed the price yet.</p></div>
  <p class="callout" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Both applications share one cache. Start with a cache miss.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 5</span><span data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span></div>
 <figcaption>An illustrative interleaving, with all cache commands succeeding. The moving card follows App A’s revision 1. P7 abbreviates <code>product:v1:north:P7:en-GB:GBP</code>. The thirty-second TTL starts when App A publishes its delayed copy. Changing deletion to an update changes step 4; the old fill can still arrive last.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>Events in order, as text</summary><ol><li>App A misses and reads GBP 20.00, revision 1, then pauses before filling.</li><li>App B commits GBP 22.00, revision 2, at the source.</li><li>App B deletes the key successfully, or writes revision 2 to it.</li><li>App A resumes and writes revision 1 with a new thirty-second TTL. The source is revision 2; the cache is revision 1.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import './race.mjs';
</script>
